  "description": "YEDWAJ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C120 H102 Dy6 N16 O36,17(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2B (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3B (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.436-3.789 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.27-106.96°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6(μ3-OH)4(L-2)2(HL-2)2(H2L-2)4]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
